00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,315
Why does this work?

2
00:00:01,315 --> 00:00:06,562
The ethoxide ion is a strong nucleophile, rich in electrons.

3
00:00:06,562 --> 00:00:13,567
It attacks the carbon carrying the iodine, and it must come in from the side exactly opposite the iodine.

4
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:18,281
This is the S N two mechanism you met in haloalkanes.

